course: dictionary
lesson: 1465
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. Castor is one of these words. In «Castor beans hold one of the strongest plant poisons, but castor oil is safe after processing», the words beans, plant and oil show that castor is a plant and an oil here, not a wheel.
explain: In «Gemini has the twin stars Castor and Pollux», the words twin stars and Gemini are your clues. A star is the meaning you need. The capital C is another clue: a name with a capital letter is the name of a star, a person or a place.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «the twin stars wheel and Pollux» make sense? No. Does «the twin stars Castor and Pollux» make sense? Yes. The right meaning always fits the whole sentence.
fact: Castor is a noun. A castor is a small wheel fixed under a chair, bed, trolley or piece of furniture so it can be moved easily. It can also be spelled caster.
fact: Castor oil is a thick, bad-tasting oil from the seeds of the castor oil plant. Children were once given it as a medicine, and many of them did not like it.
fact: Castor sugar, or caster sugar, is very fine white sugar used in baking. It dissolves quickly in cakes and meringues.
fact: Castor is also a name. It is a bright star in the Gemini constellation, named after one of the twins in Greek myths.
fact: Castor beans hold one of the strongest plant poisons, but castor oil is safe after processing and is used in medicine, soap and machine oil.
exercise: In «Gemini has the twin stars Castor and Pollux», what is Castor? | A small wheel under a chair | Very fine white sugar | A thick, bad-tasting oil | *A bright star in the Gemini constellation
exercise: Office chairs and hospital beds roll on castors. What is a castor? | A bright star in the sky | A type of sweet cake | *A small wheel fixed under furniture | A seed from a plant
exercise: What is castor oil? | A bright star in Gemini | A small wheel under a chair | Very fine white sugar for baking | *A thick, bad-tasting oil from the seeds of a plant
test: In a baking recipe, castor sugar is used. What is it? | A thick oil for cooking | Brown lumps of sugar from a cane | *Very fine white sugar that dissolves quickly | A wheel for a cake tin
test: In Greek myths, Castor is one of what? | A plant grown in gardens | *One of a pair of twins | A pair of kings | A famous racehorse
exam: Which clue in «Castor beans hold one of the strongest plant poisons, but castor oil is safe after processing» tells you castor is not a wheel? | Winter evenings | *Beans and oil | Office chairs | Hospital beds
